UniXNU 3fd6a3c: pass the board's SoC to the UFS recipes (NATIVE_UFS_<SoC>), gap G2 of macOS-Pad-6

The arm64e source-storage recipe (build-sheng-source-storage.py, which build-arm-driver.py ShengUfs runs under
arm64e) and the arm64 driver build compile NativeUfs.cpp without any SoC switch, so a SoC fork of ShengUfs (PipaUfs
for SM8250, selected by NATIVE_UFS_SM8250) is built as the SM8550 driver: its probe() looks for
"qcom,sm8550-ufshc" and never matches the board's controller. Format 1 passed the switch by hand
(build-arm-driver.py PipaUfs --sm8250).

The kernel step now exports UNIXNU_SOC from board.toml [board] soc, and both recipes add the define that
scripts/ufs_soc.py derives from it: none for SM8550 (sheng, unchanged), -DNATIVE_UFS_SM8250=1 / _SM6225=1 for the
SoCs the driver has a block for, an error for any other SoC instead of a silent SM8550 build.

Applied by macOS-Pad-6's scripts/pipa_unixnu.py to its UniXNU copy (patches/unixnu/series), and meant as the
upstream proposal. Tested on the host only (tests/test_unixnu_patches.py); no kernel or driver was built with it.

